  <cell width="340">
   <color r="255" g="248" b="178"><font name="Gulim" size="10">
    In Challenge and Campaign mode the Bonnethead Shark will be available when your zoo has reached 0.5 stars. 
   </font></color>
   <p /><font name="Gulim" size="10"> The Bonnethead Shark(Sphyrna tiburo) is a fish from the hammerheads family (Sphyrnidae), order of predator sharks (Carcharhiniformes), that lives in the Pacific and the Atlantic Ocean.
</font><p /><font name="Gulim" size="10">The Bonnethead Shark can reach the maximum length of 150 cm. The body has a streched form.
</font><p /><font name="Gulim" size="10">The fish has no sideline.
</font><p /><font name="Gulim" size="10">The Bonnethead Shark lives in salt and brakish water in a subtropic climate. The depth of the water is about 10 to 80 cm. from the surface.
</font><p /><font name="Gulim" size="10">It feeds on fish, buy hunting small fish. (it is a predator fish)
</font><p /><font name="Gulim" size="10">The Bonnethead Shark is of great importance for commercial fishing. This shark is also hunted by fishers.

</font></cell>
